ge and incumbency, but a single recent poll (D+5) and the weight of ratings justify a Democratic margin near six points.", "watch": "A late polling shift toward Kean, or a strong incumbency-driven split-ticket performance, could pull this back toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Thomas Kean Jr. (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Thomas Kean Jr. defends a New Jersey seat with an even partisan lean in what looks like a favorable year for Democrats. Challenger Rebecca Bennett has kept pace financially, raising over $4 million, and Democratic outside groups are active on her side while Kean faces little outside help. Recent polling shows Bennett up about five points, though polling in the race is thin.\n\nEvery major race rater now moves the district toward a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets price Bennett near 88-89%. Campaign coverage has centered on Kean's alignment with Trump on tariffs and Iran, his stock trades, and his House absences, themes that have defined the debates. The race remains competitive given Kean's name recognition and cash edge, but the weight of evidence favors Bennett.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.794, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7844, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8491, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8242, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8701, "margin": 6.5}]}